  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Kimchi jjigae is considered one of the most representative Korean home dishes. It developed as a way to use kimchi that had fermented beyond the point of eating fresh. The older and more sour the kimchi, the richer and more complex the stew. It is a staple of Korean family cooking throughout the country.",
