  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kimchi jjigae takes 40 minutes and serves 4. The secret is using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ripe kimchi",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kimchi-ripe"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " that has been fermenting for at least 3 to 4 weeks. Fresh kimchi makes a flat, thin stew. Old, sour kimchi makes a rich, complex one."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brown the pork belly first before adding any liquid. This step adds depth to the stew. Add "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "gochugaru",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "doenjang-jjigae-kimchi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with the pork to build extra heat and colour. Simmer for a full 20 minutes so the kimchi softens completely into the broth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
